{
  "summary": "This experiment established the performance floor for the multimodal cellular profiling study using the minimal RNA-only configuration (single profile, PCA-2000 encoder, no image encoder, no aggregation, no fusion), achieving a validation accuracy of 0.485 and F1 of 0.464. As the first completed experiment, this result serves as a baseline reference point; no comparative evidence yet exists to attribute this performance to any specific design choice. It remains uncertain whether more complex RNA encoders (e.g., scvi, scgpt), multiprofile aggregation, image modalities, or multimodal fusion can meaningfully improve upon this ~0.485 accuracy floor."
}

